  "the producer's own card is read from its file name (eNNN_) first: that is the one identity a producer cannot fail to own",
  "docstring cards are published as a set, not as ownership -- a docstring cites the studies it builds on, so the head card is often NOT this producer's own card",
  "a constant is counted as an identity only when the whole value is a card id, study id or prereg path (E461's rule: exact literal, not substring)",
